Constructed oversized rollout counterexample. Not an upstream release. Not a
production candidate. Not intended for deployment.

This fixture uses SPL Stake Pool 2.0.3 state, instruction and arithmetic helpers,
and adapts the bounded DepositSol CPI/allocation sequence from its processor.
SPL Stake Pool: Copyright Solana Labs Maintainers, Apache License 2.0.
https://github.com/solana-labs/solana-program-library/tree/master/stake-pool
The resolved published source is spl-stake-pool 2.0.3 in Cargo.lock.

Changes: derived from fixture-stake-pool-rollout-candidate, itself derived from
the Step 10B fixture-stake-pool-config-candidate. Only two instruction paths;
explicit program/account/layout validation; only ungated ten-account SOL
deposits with zero referral percentage; exact typed-prefix serialization and
unchanged trailing bytes; a stricter maximum for newly configured SOL deposit
fees (1/200). The only addition is deterministic read-only ballast data that
enlarges the ELF; it is referenced only on the rejected-instruction path. No
other protocol instruction or general-purpose Stake Pool processor is included
in dispatch.
